[Music]  pretty much everywhere you go insult the  breath of the wild can be dangerous but  some areas require more specific  preparations than others venturing out  in the middle of a thunderstorm or  scaling a snowy mountain can be deadly  if not downright impossible without the  right gear items and knowledge here's  what you need to know to survive in any  climate and be sure to subscribe for  more Zelda tips  it rains a lot in breath of the wild and  the main problem with that is rain makes  it nearly impossible to climb anything  you'll slide down most surfaces so if  you need to climb something and it  starts raining try to find a sheltered  area to build a fire and wait it out  build a fire by dropping wood with Flint  or red choo-choo jelly and striking it  with a metal weapon you can also shoot  it with a fire arrow sit by the fireside  to pastime note that you will be able to  climb very short distances during the  rain using X to jump up don't bank on it  though  if you find yourself in a thunderstorm  unequip all metal items weapons shields  and bows but don't worry about armor to  avoid being a conductor if you do end up  becoming a target you'll see sparks on  links body just before the lightning  strikes also be wary of scanning too  close to metal treasure chests or  anything  similarly attractive to lightning if  lightning strikes near you you might not  die but you will sustain a lot of damage  in some areas of Hyrule like mountain  peaks and the Gerudo desert night the  temperatures will drop to dangerously  low levels if you aren't prepared you'll  shiver and slowly lose hearts keep an  eye on the temperature gauge near your  mini-map the blue section is the danger  zone there are two ways to combat the  cold cold resistant gear like the warm  doublet and meals or elixirs that grant  you temporary cold resistance you'll  have access to both options very early  on spicy peppers warm Garner's and  summerween butterflies will all make  cold resistant dishes and elixirs and  can be found in a lot of areas check out  our video on cooking for more details in  the especially bitter cold you'll need  higher-level resistance so either  prepare a stronger meal or elixir or  equip multiple armor pieces at once be  warned though no amount of preparation  will save you from icy water use raft  tree trunks or ice blocks to cross  safely  during the day and Gerudo desert you'll  need heat resistance to survive again  keep an eye on the temperature gauge and  keep in mind that taking off your  clothes won't do anything no matter how  hot it gets in here like with cold  resistance you can either wear armor or  make dishes and elixirs that grant you  the effect for a period of time cold  darkness and chill Fionn trout are two  options for ingredients and both can be  found in and around Zoras domain inland  a roo region you can also freeze certain  ingredients like raw meat by dropping  them in the snow or icy water for a bit  to get easy heat resistant food that  also stacks in your inventory in  addition to high temperatures in the  desert there's a totally different kind  of heat around Death Mountain you'll  need the flame guard effect instead of  heat resistance or else you'll catch  fire and die pretty much instantly you  can buy fireproof elixirs from Gale at  Foothill stable to help you survive your  first trip up the volcano  last and probably the least of your  worries keep in mind that some areas  have strong winds and don't paraglide  against the wind you can however use the  wind to your advantage since it will  push round objects like remote bombs and  allow you to paraglide much farther with  that you're prepared to brave the  elements but there's a lot more to know  to get through breath of the wild so  check out our tips on how to make money  and how to care for your horse and  subscribe so you don't miss any more  zelda videos  you

